From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Przemyslaw Gorszkowski <pgorszkowski@igalia.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:45:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] device: attach deferred signal idle source to the
 thread-default context

g_io_add_watch(), g_idle_add() and g_timeout_add() always attach their
source to the global default GMainContext, not to the thread-default
one. When libmanette is used from a thread that runs its own
GMainContext pushed as thread-default (e.g. WPE WebKit / WPEFramework
on embedded platforms), the global default context is not iterated
there, so these sources are never dispatched and no gamepad events are
ever delivered.

emit_event_signal_deferred() used g_idle_add_full(), so even when raw
evdev events were read correctly, the idle callback turning them into
the device-level "button-press-event"/"absolute-axis-event"/... signals
was never invoked and consumers such as WebKit's ManetteGamepad never
saw any input.

Build the idle source with g_idle_source_new() and attach it to
g_main_context_get_thread_default().

Signed-off-by: Przemyslaw Gorszkowski <pgorszkowski@igalia.com>
---
 src/manette-device.c | 13 +++++++++----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/manette-device.c b/src/manette-device.c
index a7fc6f5..c2096e8 100644
--- a/src/manette-device.c
+++ b/src/manette-device.c
@@ -128,10 +128,15 @@ emit_event_signal_deferred (ManetteDevice *self,
                             guint          signal_id,
                             ManetteEvent  *event)
 {
-  g_idle_add_full (G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_IDLE,
-                   (GSourceFunc) manette_device_event_signal_data_emit,
-                   manette_device_event_signal_data_new (self, signal_id, event),
-                   (GDestroyNotify) manette_device_event_signal_data_free);
+  GSource *source = g_idle_source_new ();
+
+  g_source_set_priority (source, G_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_IDLE);
+  g_source_set_callback (source,
+                         (GSourceFunc) manette_device_event_signal_data_emit,
+                         manette_device_event_signal_data_new (self, signal_id, event),
+                         (GDestroyNotify) manette_device_event_signal_data_free);
+  g_source_attach (source, g_main_context_get_thread_default ());
+  g_source_unref (source);
 }
 
 static gboolean
